    <briefdescription>
<para>Variable-size counterpart of <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_collection_fixed_size" kindref="compound">MonomialCollectionFixedSize</ref></computeroutput>: pairs a <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_set_var_size" kindref="compound">MonomialSetVarSize</ref></computeroutput> with its own <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_memory_space" kindref="compound">MonomialMemorySpace</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>findOrInsert(monom)</computeroutput> allocates <computeroutput>*monom</computeroutput> ints in the arena, copies the monomial in, attempts to intern the pointer, and pops on duplicate. Same intern-or-pop pattern as the fixed-size variant with the length read from the monomial&apos;s first int. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
